The first integrity script intentionally stopped on a schema assumption: the protected Stage 3 file carries ordered IDs/classifications plus the whole inventory hash, but not duplicated spans/text fields. I’m tightening the comparison to the actual schema: ordered reconstructed IDs, ID-to-normalized-hash identity, uniqueness, and the canonical whole-inventory hash; the Stage 4 input manifest is then checked for the full span/text projection. This is a tooling correction, not a candidate discrepancy.
